    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## One-time subset build — run this per CPC area\n\nThe live search query against `patents-public-data` scans **~157 GB every run**. That is about six runs inside BigQuery's 1 TiB monthly free tier. This workflow pays that scan **once** per CPC area and writes a small clustered table the search can hit cheaply thereafter.\n\nSet `cpcPrefix` in Subset Config (e.g. C25B, A61K, C12N) and run. Re-running the same prefix deletes and rebuilds that prefix only.\n\n`maximumBytesBilled` is set to 250 GB on the populate step as a ceiling. Note that this ceiling is NOT independently verified — the n8n `dryRun` option was tested and found to execute and bill the query anyway, so treat cost controls here as unproven and watch the billing page on the first run.",
        "height": 384,
        "width": 576,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "7929d32e-7917-4c95-b094-e8eaeee937e6",
      "name": "Sticky Note 5ac4208d",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1008,
        -112
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "49f84695-9874-498d-a4a9-bc539268da15",
      "name": "Build Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        608
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "workflowInputs",
        "workflowInputs": {
          "values": [
            {
              "name": "cpcPrefix",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0ac154e5-6213-4698-a34b-67ac6a91467b",
      "name": "Validate CPC Prefix",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        304,
        416
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const raw = String(($input.first().json || {}).cpcPrefix || \"\").toUpperCase().replace(/[^A-Z0-9]/g, \"\");\nconst m = raw.match(/^([A-Z][0-9]{2}[A-Z])/);\nif (!m) {\n  throw new Error(\"Refusing to build. '\" + raw + \"' is not a valid CPC subclass. Expected four characters such as C25B or A61K. An empty or malformed prefix makes STARTS_WITH(cp.code, '') true for every row, which would insert the entire US corpus and bill for it.\");\n}\nreturn [{ json: { cpcPrefix: m[1], dataset: \"prior_art\", table: \"us_claims_by_cpc\", requestedPrefix: raw } }];"
      }
    }
